00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
The Blair Witch Project is a 1999 American found footage psychological folk horror
film written, directed, and edited by Daniel Myrick and Eduardo Sánchez.

12
00:29:27,272 --> 00:29:33,272
One of the most successful independent films of all time, it is a "found footage"
pseudo-documentary in which three students (Heather Donahue, Michael C.

13
00:31:54,545 --> 00:32:00,545
Williams, and Joshua Leonard) hike into the Appalachian Mountains near Burkittsville,
Maryland, to shoot a documentary about a local myth known as the Blair Witch.

14
00:34:21,818 --> 00:34:27,818
Myrick and Sánchez conceived of a fictional legend of the Blair Witch in 1993.

15
00:36:49,090 --> 00:36:55,090
They developed a 35-page screenplay with the dialogue to be improvised.

16
00:39:16,363 --> 00:39:22,363
A casting call advertisement on Backstage magazine was prepared by the
directors; Donahue, Williams, and Leonard were cast.

17
00:41:43,636 --> 00:41:49,636
The film entered production in October 1997, with the
principal photography lasting eight days.

18
00:44:10,909 --> 00:44:16,909
Most of the filming was done on the Greenway Trail along
Seneca Creek in Montgomery County, Maryland.

19
00:46:38,181 --> 00:46:44,181
About 20 hours of footage was shot, which was edited down to 82 minutes.

20
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
Shot on an original budget of $35,000–$60,000, the film had a final cost
of $200,000–$750,000 after post-production and marketing.

21
00:51:32,727 --> 00:51:38,727
When The Blair Witch Project premiered at the Sundance Film Festival at midnight on January 23, 1999,
its promotional marketing campaign listed the actors as either "missing" or "deceased".

22
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Due to its successful Sundance run, Artisan Entertainment bought
the film's distribution rights for $1.1 million.

23
00:56:27,272 --> 00:56:33,272
The film had a limited release on July 14 of the same year, before
expanding to a wider release starting on July 30.

24
00:58:54,545 --> 00:59:00,545
While the film received critical acclaim, audience reception was polarized.

25
01:01:21,818 --> 01:01:27,818
The Blair Witch Project was a sleeper hit that
grossed nearly $250 million worldwide.

26
01:03:49,090 --> 01:03:55,090
It is consistently listed as one of the scariest movies of all time, and was ranked the best found
footage movie of all time by editors from both IndieWire and Entertainment Weekly.

27
01:06:16,363 --> 01:06:22,363
Despite the success, the three main actors had reportedly lived in poverty.

28
01:08:43,636 --> 01:08:49,636
In 2000, they sued Artisan Entertainment claiming unfair
compensation, eventually reaching a $300,000 settlement.

29
01:11:10,909 --> 01:11:16,909
The Blair Witch Project launched a media franchise, which includes two sequels (Book
of Shadows and Blair Witch), novels, comic books, and video games.

30
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
It revived the found-footage technique and influenced similarly successful horror films
such as Paranormal Activity (2007), REC (2007) and Cloverfield (2008).

31
01:16:05,454 --> 01:16:11,454
The film explores themes of witch, legend, camping, map, supernatural.

32
01:18:32,727 --> 01:18:38,727
The tone is dark and mind_bending.
